Package: cloudscape
Type: Package
Title: Clear-Observation Availability and Cloud Analysis for Optical Satellite
    Image Time Series
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(affiliation = "Gyeongkuk National University")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", email = "cjung@gknu.ac.kr", role = "aut",
           comment = c(affiliation = "Gyeongkuk National University")))
Description: Tools for judging whether optical satellite image time series
    provide enough usable observations for a planned analysis. Archive records
    from SpatioTemporal Asset Catalogs are aggregated onto an equal-area
    analysis grid, so that counts refer to the same area for every sensor and
    latitude. Usability is recorded at an explicit evidence tier: inferred from
    scene-level cloud cover, or measured within each grid cell from producer
    quality layers ('Landsat' QA_PIXEL and 'Sentinel-2' scene classification).
    The package summarises usable counts, gaps, seasonality and cloud
    persistence, and propagates an acquisition record into the simulated error
    of phenological dates. Experimental components provide cloud-probability
    algorithms, including a threshold baseline and a decision cascade following
    Zhu and Woodcock (2012) <doi:10.1016/j.rse.2011.10.028>, geometric
    cloud-shadow projection with separation of terrain shadow, and synthetic
    cloud simulation for benchmarking. Every statistic carries its unit, sample
    size and denominator, which are validated on construction.
